lines.extend(['','These ALK5 structures were previously used for protocol development; they are not an untouched external validation set. All RMSDs are symmetry-corrected heavy-atom values without alignment.','', '## Exploratory ranking','','Mean rank combines per-engine ranks, not raw energies. Lower is better. No combined affinity is inferred.','', '| Candidate | Vina score | DOCK6 score | Mean rank | AMES | hERG | DILI | ALK5 similarity |','|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|'])
for row in s['ranked']:
 d=row['selection_data'];t=d['toxicity'];lines.append(f"| {row['name']} | {row['vina_score']:.2f} | {row['dock6_score']:.2f} | {row['mean_rank']:.2f} | {t['AMES']:.3f} | {t['hERG']:.3f} | {t['DILI']:.3f} | {d['max_alk5_active_tanimoto']:.3f} |")
lines.extend(['','## Diverse structures for human review','','After a post hoc potential-stereo audit, the first five distinct scaffolds without unresolved stereogenic units in the exploratory rank summary are: '+', '.join(s['review_shortlist'])+'. They are a review set, not experimentally validated leads.','', '![Review structures](review_structures.png)','', '## Limits and next interpretation','','A subsequent RDKit FindPotentialStereo audit flagged candidate_17 (two potential tetrahedral units) and candidates_07, candidate_16 and candidate_20 (unspecified double-bond stereo). The initial legacy chiral-center filter missed these cases. All four remain in the locked primary analysis, and were excluded only from the exploratory human-review shortlist; this is a documented protocol limitation, not a changed 20-member selection.','The ADMET model outputs are uncalibrated screening estimates, not measured toxicities. The same model both selected and evaluated the set; an external assay is required to validate any safety improvement. Similarity to 70 known ALK5 actives is modest and does not establish target binding. This small, similarity-selected set and its cross-engine correlation do not quantify enrichment or prospective hit rate. There is no exhaustive tautomer/protonation sampling, no receptor dynamics, no experimental target engagement, and no comprehensive novelty or patent search. BRENK alerts remain warnings and are included in the CSV.','', 'The generator was not retrained. Results and failures are retained for every locked candidate. Candidate IDs refer to selection order before docking, not a biological potency ranking. The earlier 12-candidate experiment remains a separate dataset.','', '## Reproduction and sources','','- Run scripts/generate_admet_first_alk5.py, then dock_admet_first_alk5.py, then summarize_admet_first_alk5.py in the WSL aipharma environment with the saved input files.','- Selection protocol, raw generation records, all ADMET outputs, baseline recomputation and lock hash are in results/.','- Per-candidate preparation, conformers, docking inputs, raw poses, logs and scores are in docking/.','- [ADMET-AI source and version guidance](https://github.com/swansonk14/admet_ai)','- [DOCK6 manual](https://dock.compbio.ucsf.edu/DOCK_6/dock6_manual.htm)','- Library versions: '+json.dumps(protocol['versions'])])
(root/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
